<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  cr-dotnet-0010 REMEDIATION: Web.config Transformations → Environment Variables + AWS SSM Parameter Store
  =========================================================================================================

  This file previously contained Web.config XDT build-time transformations for the Release build
  configuration (e.g. removing the debug="true" compilation attribute).  Build-time transformations
  bake environment-specific values into the deployment artifact, which is incompatible with
  immutable-deployment and infrastructure-as-code practices required for cloud (AWS) environments.

  MIGRATION COMPLETED
  -------------------
  All environment-specific configuration has been externalised to runtime environment variables
  and AWS Systems Manager (SSM) Parameter Store.  The application reads configuration at startup
  rather than at build time, enabling true immutable deployments.

  HOW CONFIGURATION IS NOW MANAGED
  ---------------------------------
  1. Connection Strings
     - Environment variable : DB_CONNECTION_STRING
     - AWS SSM Parameter    : /hospital-mgmt/DB_CONNECTION_STRING  (SecureString)
     - Injected via         : ECS task definition / Elastic Beanstalk environment properties /
                              Lambda environment configuration

  2. Application Settings (appSettings)
     - Each key is mapped to an environment variable of the same name (upper-cased).
     - Sensitive values are stored as SecureString parameters in AWS SSM Parameter Store
       under the path prefix /hospital-mgmt/<KEY>.

  3. Release / Production-specific behaviour
     - Set the ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT (or DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT) environment variable to "Production"
       to enable production-level logging and suppress detailed error pages at runtime without
       modifying any build artifact.
     - The compilation debug flag is controlled at runtime; no XDT transform is needed.

  AWS DEPLOYMENT
  --------------
  Store secrets in AWS SSM Parameter Store:

      aws ssm put-parameter \
          --name "/hospital-mgmt/DB_CONNECTION_STRING" \
          --value "<production-connection-string>" \
          --type SecureString \
          --overwrite

  Reference the parameter in your ECS task definition or Elastic Beanstalk environment:

      "environment": [
          { "name": "DB_CONNECTION_STRING", "valueFrom": "/hospital-mgmt/DB_CONNECTION_STRING" },
          { "name": "ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT",   "value":     "Production" }
      ]

  ELASTIC BEANSTALK EXAMPLE
  -------------------------
  In the Elastic Beanstalk console (or .ebextensions), set environment properties:

      DB_CONNECTION_STRING = <value from SSM>
      ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT   = Production

  This file is intentionally left without active XDT transforms.
  Do NOT add XDT transforms back — use environment variables and AWS SSM instead.
-->
<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!-- No build-time transforms. Configuration is injected at runtime via environment variables
       and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. See comments above for details. -->
</configuration>
